    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d336">

                <pb facs="1209" n="1185" sameAs="frus:frus1946v02/pg1185"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">C.F.M. Files: Lot
                    M–88: Box 2079: CFM Documents</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Proposals by the Soviet
                            Delegation to the Council of Foreign
                            Ministers</hi><anchor n="37" xml:id="d336-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        CFM(46) (NY) 15 Revised<anchor n="38"
                            xml:id="d336-f2"/></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">New
                                York</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1946-11-17"
                            >November 17, 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Peace Treaty With Italy</hi></p>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Article</hi> 16</p>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">amendments of soviet delegation
                        to paragraph 11 of the french proposal</hi><anchor n="39" xml:id="d336-f3"
                    /></p>
                <p>11. <hi rendition="#italic">Free Port and Economic Questions</hi></p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Paragraph 11a</hi>)—accept draft of United States and
                    United Kingdom Delegations (see Article 30 of draft provisions for Free Port)
                    with the following changes: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>. A Free Port shall be established in the
                            Free Territory and shall be administered on the basis of the provisions
                            of an international instrument <hi rendition="#italic">drawn up by the
                                Council of Foreign Ministers and approved by the Security
                                Council</hi>. (omit words “controlling the Free Port of
                            Trieste”)</p>
                        <p>The Government of the Free Territory shall enact all necessary
                            legislation and take all necessary steps to implement the provisions of
                            such instrument.”</p></quote></p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Paragraph 11b</hi>)—accept the draft of the French
                    Delegations with the following changes: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>) The establishment of free zones under
                            the exclusive jurisdiction of any country, <hi rendition="#italic">with
                                the exception of neighboring countries</hi>, is incompatible with
                            the Statute of the Free Territory and of the Free Port.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Paragraphs 11c</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">and
                    d</hi>)—Paragraph 11<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi> is accepted without amendment
                    provided the following wording is adopted for Paragraph 11<hi
                        rendition="#italic">d</hi>).</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“<hi rendition="#italic">d</hi>) In order to enesure favorable conditions for
                        the economic development of the Free Territory of Trieste economic
                        collaboration shall be established between the Free Territory and Yugoslavia
                        (customs union, joint administration of the railroads of the Free Territory
                        of Trieste, etc.)”</p>
                </quote>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d336-f1" n="37" type="source" xml:id="d336-f1-content">
                <p>This paper was considered by the Council of Foreign Ministers at its 4th and 5th
                    Informal Meetings, November 20 and November 21; for the United States Delegation
                    Minutes of those meetings, see <ref target="#pg1200">pp. 1200</ref> and <ref
                        target="#pg1215">1215</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d336-f2" n="38" xml:id="d336-f2-content">
                <p>This paper is virtually identical with the original draft (CFM(46)(NY) 15, November 17, 1946), except for
                    a slight revision in sub-paragraph <hi rendition="#italic">d</hi>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d336-f3" n="39" xml:id="d336-f3-content">
                <p>The paragraph under reference is that of the French proposal for article 16 of
                    the Draft Peace Treaty with Italy as included in the Record of Recommendations
                    of the Peace Conference, <ref target="frus1946v04#pg_895">vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">iv</hi>, p. 895</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
